From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gregory Mitchell <me@gmitch215.xyz>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:58:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wasm: raise the page allocator's max order to 14

Without an MMU every anonymous mmap is one physically contiguous block
from the page allocator. The generic MAX_PAGE_ORDER of 10 capped a
program's largest allocation at 4 MiB, and Lua's gc test failed to
allocate 4 MiB plus a page with 47 MB free. Order 14 is 64 MiB, the
kernel's RAM at boot. arc, arm and nios2 set ARCH_FORCE_MAX_ORDER the
same way.
---
 arch/wasm/Kconfig | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/wasm/Kconfig b/arch/wasm/Kconfig
--- a/arch/wasm/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/wasm/Kconfig
@@ -123,4 +123,13 @@ config PGTABLE_LEVELS
 	int
 	default 2
 
+config ARCH_FORCE_MAX_ORDER
+	int "Order of maximal physically contiguous allocations"
+	default "14"
+	help
+	  Without an MMU every anonymous mmap is one physically contiguous
+	  block from the page allocator, so the largest order is the largest
+	  allocation a program can make. The generic default of 10 caps it at
+	  4 MiB; 14 allows 64 MiB, the kernel's RAM at boot.
+
 endmenu
